## Why My Previous Plan Was Partly Wrong

I was advising from a **working professional's** lens. For someone with a job, projects > education. But you're a **student** — your situation is:

| Your Reality | What That Means For The Site |
|---|---|
| Undergrad at University of Dhaka | **Education IS your primary credential.** Keep it on the home page. |
| No corporate work | There's only ONE section for activities. "Leadership & Experience" is correct. No need for a "Work" section. |
| Projects are gamedev/webdev, career is accounting | **Projects are a separate facet**, not your professional identity. Keep them on `/projects` for curious explorers. |
| Site copied from LinkedIn | The resume structure is mostly right — it just needs better **visual presentation** and a **color identity**. |

### What I Got Wrong:
- ❌ Removing education from the home page
- ❌ Adding featured projects to the home page
- ❌ Saying "it's a data dump" — for a student CV, showing education + leadership + credentials IS the right content

### What I Got Right:
- ✅ Needs a signature color (you confirmed: warm solaris)
- ✅ Needs visual media / placeholders
- ✅ Needs SEO fundamentals (favicon, OG, robots.txt)
- ✅ The "One Shell, Multiple Faces" concept is strong
- ✅ Type safety and CSS foundation need work
- ✅ `globals.css` is empty and needs proper custom styles

