## On "Experience" vs "Work" — Your Question Answered

> *"What's the difference between experience and work sections? Why do we need two?"*

**You don't.** Here's the distinction:

| Section Name | Who Uses It | Contains |
|---|---|---|
| "Work Experience" | Professionals with jobs | Company names, job titles, corporate roles |
| "Leadership & Experience" | Students / community leaders | Organizations, volunteer roles, clubs |
| "Work" | Same as above, shorter name | Same |

For you, **"Leadership & Experience"** is perfect. It correctly frames your community organizations (Team J, Morning Riders, Al Hikmah Society, আলোকিত লাইব্রেরী) as **experience** without pretending they're corporate jobs.

When you graduate and get a job, you'll add a "Work" section above this, and rename this to "Leadership & Community" or "Activities." But for now — one section is right.

